## 30. SEARCH, FEED, AND CACHE CONSISTENCY

Define consistency requirements for database records, caches, search indexes, and feed results.

When content changes audience or is deleted:

- Recheck authorization at read time.
- Invalidate relevant caches.
- Remove or update indexed records.
- Prevent stale private content from appearing in recommendations.
- Handle delayed background cleanup safely.
- Preserve privacy during indexing and retries.

Define which data can be cached publicly and which must remain private.

Do not assume cache keys alone provide authorization.

Use bounded cache lifetimes and documented invalidation rules.

Test behavior when Redis, the search index, or an asynchronous consumer is temporarily unavailable.

