Use real database persistence for implemented features.

Run the relevant commands and tests in the available environment, and report their actual output.

If a dependency, credential, external service, or infrastructure requirement is unavailable, document the blocker and implement a safe integration boundary without claiming completion.

Make reasonable decisions, minimize unnecessary questions, and keep the project buildable after every milestone.

FINAL OBJECTIVE:

Build Subhu as a cohesive, original, secure, privacy-aware, accessible, maintainable, and reliable social networking platform.

Prioritize working end-to-end functionality, verified security, reliable data processing, user control, and sustainable engineering over the number of features claimed.

The quality of Subhu must be measured by verified behavior, not by the size of the codebase or the number of screens generated.